                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The time spent travelling at 60 km/h is $(3-x)$ hours. The two distances add to 350 km.\n$$\\begin{align*}120x+60(3-x)&=350\\\\120x+180-60x&=350\\\\60x+180&=350\\\\60x&=170\\\\x&=\\frac{17}{6}\\end{align*}$$\nThe time spent travelling at 120 km/h is $\\dfrac{17}{6}$ hours.",
